      "stageRecord": "Spanish also permits transitive vivir in the sense of experiencing something. With a discourse-recoverable theme, the exact input can consequently mean that it is experienced well here. Unlike the ordinary impersonal reading, this reading requires an understood experience, life, or comparable theme; the sentence alone does not identify that referent. The silent referential NP is first placed as the complement of V and receives the internal theme theta-role there. No external argument NP is projected in this passive derivation. Bien modifies the experiencing event as a manner adjunct, and aquí is an outer locative VP adjunct. Finite I is specified as present and third-person singular. Se remains a separate clitic at this stage; passive Case absorption and suppression of the external argument will be established when it attaches to the finite verbal head.",
