      "stageRecord": "Vive first raises from V to I and leaves a locally bound, antecedent-governed head trace. Se then attaches to the left of that finite head. In this passive analysis, attachment establishes the suppression of the external experiencer as a syntactic argument and the absorption of structural accusative Case. An implicit experiencer remains semantically available, but it is not an arbitrary subject NP. Se is therefore a passive clitic rather than a reflexive argument governed by Principle A. The theme remains in the complement position in this intermediate workspace: it has its theta-role but cannot receive structural accusative Case. Recording this state separately makes passive formation precede the theme's subsequent A-movement. The finite lexical word remains vive; abstract I has no independent phonological realization.",
      "statement": "Form the finite passive-se head while leaving the theme in its original object position.",
