      "stageRecord": "The silent theme moves from the previously displayed complement of V to the previously unoccupied Spec-IP. Its original position becomes an NP trace. This A-chain preserves the single theme theta-role assigned in the object position; Spec-IP contributes Case, not another theta-role. The subject binds its object trace within the clause, and the trace remains lexically governed by the verbal position, satisfying the requirements on an NP trace. Finite I assigns nominative Case to the raised subject and agrees with it in third-person singular. Spanish finite inflection formally licenses the null subject, while discourse must recover its reference. Unlike the impersonal analysis, the agreement here is with a referential singular theme, not an arbitrary human subject. A silent declarative C then embeds the completed IP. The four pronounced terminals are exactly Se, vive, bien, and aquí.",
      "statement": "Raise and license the silent theme subject, completing the passive reading.",
